# Settings > Updates > Packages (report 047 P4) on the Pi 5's capture: 244 upgrades (234 safe, 8 launcher libraries, the
# rest boot chain), 23 kept back by apt (they stay in "Needs the terminal"). The dense list keeps its rows and the same
# actions: "Upgrade N packages" first; libcurl3t64-gnutls pulls curl and libcurl4t64 (one source): it joins the launcher
# libraries, so the plan has 233 and the confirmation says 1 more waits; with the libraries on, 242. On the small screens
# the text block is longer than its room: Down on the first row scrolls it first. Keys only. Review only: no golden.
title updates upgrade pi5
review
sizes 640x480 480x800 480x640 720x720 1280x800 480x320
@480x800,480x640 profile pda
env APPLAUNCH_DEV 0
env HARNESS_APPS missing
env HARNESS_SUDO ok
apps Settings CLI SSH Calculator
clock 20:30 2026-11-01
wifi 70
bt on
update net on
update build 0.9.2 release arm64
update answer releases-real.json
apt board pi5
apt lists-age 1
home
launch Settings
wait 300
key UP
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
wait 3000
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 2000
shot upgrade_pi5_list
expect_text "Upgrade 233 packages"
key DOWN
key ENTER
wait 600
shot upgrade_pi5_confirm
expect_text "Launcher libraries (9)"
expect_unclipped "Launcher libraries (9)" "Upgrade now" "Cancel"
key DOWN
key DOWN
key DOWN
wait 400
shot upgrade_pi5_confirm_scrolled
key HOME
key UP
key UP
key UP
key ENTER
wait 400
shot upgrade_pi5_confirm_libraries
expect_text "Included: the launcher runs on these"
key ESC
wait 400
shot upgrade_pi5_back
expect_text "Upgrade 233 packages"
key ESC
key ESC
wait 300
